{
 "total": 39.679,
 "frases": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "a": 0.15,
   "b": 2.379,
   "texto": "Your deck boards are curling up like potato chips!",
   "h": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "a": 2.499,
   "b": 4.951,
   "texto": "Hit like and follow. Flo says it's all about the bark!",
   "h": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "a": 5.071,
   "b": 8.092,
   "texto": "Everybody knows it! Bark side up, and boards never cup!",
   "h": 1
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "a": 8.212,
   "b": 10.999,
   "texto": "The bark side helps a little. But that's not the real problem.",
   "h": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "a": 11.119,
   "b": 15.663,
   "texto": "Your deck sits a few inches off wet dirt. The bottom stays damp, and the sun dries the top.",
   "h": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "a": 15.783,
   "b": 19.276,
   "texto": "The wet side swells, the dry side shrinks, and the board cups.",
   "h": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "a": 19.396,
   "b": 20.78,
   "texto": "So the bark thing is a myth?",
   "h": 1
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "a": 20.9,
   "b": 24.199,
   "texto": "Mostly. Experts say the moisture under the deck matters a lot more.",
   "h": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "a": 24.319,
   "b": 27.431,
   "texto": "Give it room to breathe. Open the sides so air can flow underneath.",
   "h": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "a": 27.551,
   "b": 30.891,
   "texto": "And put gravel over a ground cover, so the dirt can't wet the boards.",
   "h": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "a": 31.011,
   "b": 33.976,
   "texto": "Fine. My deck gets a breeze, not a bark lecture.",
   "h": 1
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "a": 34.096,
   "b": 37.493,
   "texto": "Bark side up, or airflow underneath? Team Norm or Team Flo?",
   "h": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "a": 37.613,
   "b": 39.679,
   "texto": "Follow for more backyard builds that won't fail!",
   "h": 0
  }
 ],
